{"4993060": {"success": true, "data": {"type": "game", "name": "HR Hell", "steam_appid": 4993060, "required_age": 0, "is_free": false, "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Congratulations on your new role in HR. Unfortunately, the role is in Hell, your staff are demons, and the coffee has opinions.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A demon quit last month, died shortly after, and has now returned as a ghost to request the exit interview she never got. Do you: listen sincerely, rush her out, or hire the ghost back, part-time? <strong>That's one case. Your inbox has hundreds.</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>It's your worst Monday, forever.</strong> Each day, impossible cases land on your desk — possessed printers, soul-quota shortfalls, an intern who opened a portal in the supply closet &quot;to hit a deadline.&quot; Read the case, pick one response, and live with it. Every decision moves your Budget, Morale, Reputation, Stress, and Favor — and you cannot keep them all happy.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Survive five days and the Board reviews your numbers.</strong> Pass, and you choose a perk — some last a week, some last the rest of your contract. Some weeks the Company also hauls you into a Corporate Trial to defend your record — yes, including the ghost — where every answer is a trade-off and the verdict merely decides guilty <i>of what</i>. Fall short twice and the floor opens beneath you.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4993060/extras/047f7729b4e167c9dfc8f82cd4435fe9.poster.avif?t=1787600071\" width=1170 height=702 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4993060/extras/047f7729b4e167c9dfc8f82cd4435fe9.webm?t=1787600071\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4993060/extras/047f7729b4e167c9dfc8f82cd4435fe9.mp4?t=1787600071\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Then you clock in again. There are thirteen known ways out of this job. You'll find maybe one.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Features</strong></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >☄️ <strong>A darkly funny office in Hell</strong> — handle hundreds of absurd HR cases, from thermostat wars and dress codes limiting horn height to 18 inches to three managers who report to each other in a circle, where decisions go in and never come out</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >⚖️ <strong>You are the evidence</strong> — Corporate Trials cite your actual rulings; demons you helped testify for you, demons you burned testify against you</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >🎭 <strong>A cast that remembers you</strong> — the demons you help or burn keep score, and turn up again when it matters. Some storylines run deeper: Brenda the intern may quietly be running Hell, and Pemberton the Eternal Auditor never closes a case. You won't meet everyone in one run.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >🃏 <strong>Build your management style</strong> — perks and policies let you rule by fear, kindness, or pure profit</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >💀 <strong>13 endings to discover</strong> — escape to Heaven, get promoted to Vice President of Eternal Torment, hand your empire to Brenda, or burn out (literally)</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >⏱️ <strong>One contract, start to finish</strong> — 30 days, one sitting if you're brave. Three difficulties: PROBATION spells out what each choice will cost you. STANDARD tells you nothing. DAMNATION also hides what the Board wants, and offers no second chance.</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4993060/extras/e05914d6b382cd54be48a7bce7ae9fee.poster.avif?t=1787600071\" width=1170 height=714 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4993060/extras/e05914d6b382cd54be48a7bce7ae9fee.webm?t=1787600071\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4993060/extras/e05914d6b382cd54be48a7bce7ae9fee.mp4?t=1787600071\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The position is open because the last manager left through the floor. <strong>Hell is hiring.</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p>", "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Congratulations on your new role in HR. Unfortunately, the role is in Hell, your staff are demons, and the coffee has opinions.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A demon quit last month, died shortly after, and has now returned as a ghost to request the exit interview she never got. Do you: listen sincerely, rush her out, or hire the ghost back, part-time? <strong>That's one case. Your inbox has hundreds.</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>It's your worst Monday, forever.</strong> Each day, impossible cases land on your desk — possessed printers, soul-quota shortfalls, an intern who opened a portal in the supply closet &quot;to hit a deadline.&quot; Read the case, pick one response, and live with it. Every decision moves your Budget, Morale, Reputation, Stress, and Favor — and you cannot keep them all happy.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Survive five days and the Board reviews your numbers.</strong> Pass, and you choose a perk — some last a week, some last the rest of your contract. Some weeks the Company also hauls you into a Corporate Trial to defend your record — yes, including the ghost — where every answer is a trade-off and the verdict merely decides guilty <i>of what</i>. Fall short twice and the floor opens beneath you.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4993060/extras/047f7729b4e167c9dfc8f82cd4435fe9.poster.avif?t=1787600071\" width=1170 height=702 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4993060/extras/047f7729b4e167c9dfc8f82cd4435fe9.webm?t=1787600071\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4993060/extras/047f7729b4e167c9dfc8f82cd4435fe9.mp4?t=1787600071\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Then you clock in again. There are thirteen known ways out of this job. You'll find maybe one.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Features</strong></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >☄️ <strong>A darkly funny office in Hell</strong> — handle hundreds of absurd HR cases, from thermostat wars and dress codes limiting horn height to 18 inches to three managers who report to each other in a circle, where decisions go in and never come out</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >⚖️ <strong>You are the evidence</strong> — Corporate Trials cite your actual rulings; demons you helped testify for you, demons you burned testify against you</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >🎭 <strong>A cast that remembers you</strong> — the demons you help or burn keep score, and turn up again when it matters. Some storylines run deeper: Brenda the intern may quietly be running Hell, and Pemberton the Eternal Auditor never closes a case. You won't meet everyone in one run.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >🃏 <strong>Build your management style</strong> — perks and policies let you rule by fear, kindness, or pure profit</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >💀 <strong>13 endings to discover</strong> — escape to Heaven, get promoted to Vice President of Eternal Torment, hand your empire to Brenda, or burn out (literally)</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >⏱️ <strong>One contract, start to finish</strong> — 30 days, one sitting if you're brave. Three difficulties: PROBATION spells out what each choice will cost you. STANDARD tells you nothing. DAMNATION also hides what the Board wants, and offers no second chance.</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4993060/extras/e05914d6b382cd54be48a7bce7ae9fee.poster.avif?t=1787600071\" width=1170 height=714 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4993060/extras/e05914d6b382cd54be48a7bce7ae9fee.webm?t=1787600071\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4993060/extras/e05914d6b382cd54be48a7bce7ae9fee.mp4?t=1787600071\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The position is open because the last manager left through the floor. <strong>Hell is hiring.</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p>", "short_description": "A ghost wants her exit interview. Do you listen, refuse or hire her back part-time? You're Hell's HR manager: hundreds of absurd cases, questionable policies, a Board watching your numbers, and a court that quotes your own decisions back to you. Survive 30 days. Find one of 13 ways out.", "supported_languages": "English<strong>*</strong><br><strong>*</strong>languages with full audio support", "header_image": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4993060/05f5e4e7bcc80967d6af3048dff9da54aec5fdd1